The whole "look at log to find details about bones" is a pretty
interesting issue from a game design point of view; it's not possible in
vanilla (except by asking the player who died, or by finding your own
bones and remembering and referring to your notes), but the dumplogs
definitely generally add to the game, so removing them would be a
mistake. I've already taken steps towards reducing abuse in AceHack and
NetHack 4 (items discovered in a bones pile will be sorted by
alphabetical order of possibly unidentified name in the game
encountering them, so at least you can't distinguish two unidentified
wands from each other by looking at the dumplog); I'd like to make bones
further impossible to abuse along these lines, but it's not entirely
clear how. (Or just encourage playing without bones; bones are pretty
abusable even without dumplog looking, because the levels they're on are
rarely particularly deadly, and the loot approximately doubles your
character's selection of possessions.)

